# Constants of the bridge to "fluid_styled_content".
#
# The bridge deliberately declares none of its own. It changes which templates
# render the classic content elements, not what they are configured with: the
# theme's own constants come from "Configuration/TypoScript/constants.typoscript"
# by way of the theme's set or its static include, and that extension's
# "styles.*" constants come from its own.
#
# The file exists anyway, and is not an oversight. Both delivery mechanisms
# append a file name to the registered directory - the static include through
# the path passed to "addStaticFile()", and on v13 the site set through
# "typoscript:" in "config.yaml" - so the constants half of this include
# resolves to this file rather than to nothing.
#
# Its sibling "Configuration/TypoScript/Static/constants.typoscript" is NOT
# there for the same reason, and the difference is worth stating rather than
# glossing: that file carries a guarded "@import" of the theme's real
# constants, behind the
# "[not ('sbuerk/theme-extension-development' in site('sets'))]" condition that
# stops a site using the set from parsing them a second time. It earns its
# keep; this one is a true placeholder. What the two have in common is only
# that "StaticTypoScriptIncludeTest" holds both directories to shipping both
# files.
